# Line endings are checked out as LF on every platform.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. With core.autocrlf=true and no attributes, git rewrote the working tree to
# CRLF on every checkout and merge. Many tests read source files and match them with regexes that
# end a one-line function at `}\n` — those stop matching against `}\r\n`, so `npm test` reported
# four failures that had nothing to do with the code and would vanish again after the next commit.
# A suite whose result depends on which git command ran last cannot be trusted to catch anything.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
